      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the LLM Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google's Generative AI for the LLM. My next step will be to code the implementation within `answer_with_context.py` to call the generative AI service. I want to build in error handling to prevent issues in the external API from breaking the Python program.\n\n\n**Implementing the LLM Call**\n\nI'm now focused on the concrete implementation in `answer_with_context.py`. I'm starting with the essential steps: importing `google.generativeai` and defining the core function that will interface with the LLM, taking a question and context as input. I'm choosing the `gemini-pro` model as the target for this specific implementation. I'll make sure it handles any issues with the LLM API call.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818657659,
          "start": 1789818655573
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9815355001QMxCvtwQa3S1T6",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9814e0400144BDn05DnITt3A",
      "session_id": "ses_f467eb219ffety1ea9AICUVHS0",
      "time_created": 1789818655573,
      "time_updated": 1789818657660
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "GC56KXjLLZIAH0qL",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import google.generativeai as genai\nimport os\n\ndef answer_with_context(question: str, context: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calls a hosted LLM (Google Gemini Pro) to answer a question using provided context.\n\n    Args:\n        question: The question to ask the LLM.\n        context: The context to provide to the LLM for answering the question.\n\n    Returns:\n        The LLM's answer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Configure the Google Generative AI client\n    # Ensure GOOGLE_API_KEY environment variable is set\n    genai.configure(api_key=os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"))\n\n    # Initialize the Generative Model\n    model = genai.GenerativeModel('gemini-pro')\n\n    # Construct the prompt for the LLM\n    prompt = f\"\"\"\n    Context:\n    {context}\n\n    Question:\n    {question}\n\n    Answer the question truthfully based on the provided context. If the answer is not available in the context, state that you don't have enough information.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Generate content using the model\n    response = model.generate_content(prompt)\n\n    # Return the text from the response\n    return response.text.strip()\n\n",
            "filePath": "answer_with_context.py"
          },
