      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing the LLM Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward using Google Cloud's Generative AI services. Specifically, I'm leaning toward either Vertex AI or the Gemini API as the primary LLM provider for the Python script. I will need to consider their respective strengths and ease of integration for this project.\n\n\n**Defining the Script's Structure**\n\nI'm starting the `extract_json.py` file. The initial focus is on setting up the basic structure. I'm importing the `google.generativeai` library and setting the LLM provider to `gemini-pro`. Dummy environment variables will hold the API key. The next step is crafting the prompt that will instruct the LLM to extract JSON.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818650945,
          "start": 1789818647033
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98131f9001dO6P2E62JycomH",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9812ca6001KJn7rlu8EP6YKG",
      "session_id": "ses_f467ed37bffexJXLaeWnrMlQAY",
      "time_created": 1789818647033,
      "time_updated": 1789818650945
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "CL6EOYQ77ArufBNp",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import google.generativeai as genai\nimport os\nimport json\n\ndef extract_json_from_text(text: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calls a hosted LLM (Google Gemini) to extract structured JSON from text.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        genai.configure(api_key=os.environ[\"GEMINI_API_KEY\"])\n    except KeyError:\n        raise ValueError(\"GEMINI_API_KEY environment variable not set.\")\n\n    model = genai.GenerativeModel('gemini-pro')\n\n    prompt = f\"\"\"\n    Extract any structured JSON object from the following text.\n    If no JSON object is found, return an empty JSON object {{}}.\n\n    Text:\n    \"\"\"\n    {text}\n    \"\"\"\n\n    Please return only the JSON object, nothing else.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    response = model.generate_content(prompt)\n    \n    # Assuming the model's response directly contains the JSON string\n    try:\n        json_string = response.text.strip()\n        if json_string.startswith(\"```json\") and json_string.endswith(\"```\"):\n            json_string = json_string[7:-3].strip()\n        \n        # Attempt to load the JSON. If it fails, return empty dict.\n        return json.loads(json_string)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        print(f\"Warning: Could not decode JSON from response: {response.text}\")\n        return {}\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n        return {}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage\n    os.environ[\"GEMINI_API_KEY\"] = \"YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY\" # Replace with your actual API key\n\n    text_with_json = \"Here is some data: {\"name\": \"Alice\", \"age\": 30, \"city\": \"New York\"}. And some more text.\"\n    extracted_data = extract_json_from_text(text_with_json)\n    print(\"Extracted JSON:\", extracted_data)\n\n    text_without_json = \"This text does not contain any JSON data.\"\n    extracted_data_2 = extract_json_from_text(text_without_json)\n    print(\"Extracted JSON (no JSON):\", extracted_data_2)\n\n    text_with_invalid_json = \"This text has some malformed json: {name: 'Bob', age: 25}.\"\n    extracted_data_3 = extract_json_from_text(text_with_invalid_json)\n    print(\"Extracted JSON (invalid JSON):\", extracted_data_3)\n",
            "filePath": "extract_json.py"
          },
